# No commits

Never run `git add`, `git commit`, `git push`, or any other Git command that records, sends, or rewrites history.

Even if a plan, spec, skill, or suggested commit message says otherwise: edit the files and stop. The user commits.

```text
# ❌ BAD
git add README.md
git commit -m "docs: add README"

# ✅ GOOD
# Write/edit the files and leave the working tree unstaged
```

Exception: only run write Git commands if the user explicitly asks in that message (for example “commit this”).
